Upstream adds tag to a new rule *://*.shop.example.net/*: Compile fails
naming (tag, include). It passes once an overlay Keep covers the include,
or once the pair is exempted with a reason; an exemption without a reason
fails Schema.
-- ops --
jappend rules/brave/clean-urls.json [] {"include": ["*://*.shop.example.net/*"], "exclude": [], "params": ["tag"]}
relock
run Compile
fail keep coverage: brave/clean-urls strips "tag" at *://*.shop.example.net/*
jappend rules/overlay/overlay.json [{"id": "amazon-affiliate-keep"}, "include"] "*://*.shop.example.net/*"
run Compile
nofail keep coverage
jremove rules/overlay/overlay.json [{"id": "amazon-affiliate-keep"}, "include"] "*://*.shop.example.net/*"
run Compile
fail keep coverage: brave/clean-urls strips "tag" at *://*.shop.example.net/*
-- ops --
append testdata/keep-coverage-exempt.txt "tag *://*.shop.example.net/* # fixture: a first-party tracking tag, not an affiliate one\n"
run Compile
nofail keep coverage
run Schema
pass
-- ops --
replace testdata/keep-coverage-exempt.txt " # fixture: a first-party tracking tag, not an affiliate one" ""
run Schema
fail "tag *://*.shop.example.net/*" does not match
